  "description": "Demolition of the garage and extension to 136 Saxon Avenue and erection of a two-storey 3-bedroom house extension with associated parking and access.",
  "site_name": "Garages adj 36",
  "last_updated_by": "Northgate M3",
  "decision_target_date": "28/11/2007",
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": "TW13 5LU",
  "street_name": "Saxon Avenue",
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Major all other major developments",
  "lapsed_date": "27/11/2010",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the extension hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building.",
    "Condition : 3 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 4 - The  bath room window formed in the first floorsouth elevation  shall be obscure glazed, hinged to open inwards and shall not be repaired or replaced otherwise than with obscured glazing.",
    "Condition : 5 - Notwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development Order) 1995 (or any order revoking or re-enacting that order) no enlargement of the premises or any additional structures/buildings within the curtilage of the site shall be carried out.",
    "Condition : 6 - Before commencement of operations, a scheme shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority to cover the following matters:\r\n(i)\tany external illumination of the site\r\n(ii)\tmeasures to ensure that all mud and other loose materials are not carried on the wheels and chassis of any vehicles leaving the site; and\r\n(iii)\tmeasures to minimise dust nuisance caused by the operations and to ensure that no dust or other debris is carried on to the adjoining properties.\r\nThe scheme so approved should be fully implemented.\r\n",
    "Condition : 7 - No demolition or construction work shall take place on the site except between the hours of 8.am  to 18.00  on Mondays to Friday inclusive, and from 08.00 am to 13.00 on \r\nSaturdays and no work at any time on Sundays or and Public Holidays without the prior agreement of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 8 - The garage or car parking accommodation shown on drawing No. SAX100 REVA shall be provided before the dwelling to which it relates is occupied and thereafter it shall not be used for any purpose other than the parking of vehicles.",
    "Condition : 9 - A splay of 2.4m x 2.4m shall be provided on each side of the access, the depth measured from the back of the footway and the widths outwards from the edges of the access, and no fence, wall or other obstruction to visibility exceeding 0.6m in height above the surface of the adjoining highway shall be erected within the areas of such splays.",
    "Condition : 10 - A landscaping scheme for the front garden shall be submitted\r\n      to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. The approved \r\n      details shall be implemented in full before the house is occupied\r\n"
  ],
